From d8c7fbe9931ad093d38dea13383eea77541bd0ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 05:11:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: the serializer, the CM v4.0 conversion, the
 packer and the direct way's hooks written again

The last four files of the Dolby Vision module under GPL-3.0-or-later held code of CroqueMr's Dolby
Vision fork of LibreELEC (kodi-9990), whose author offers his original contributions under
GPL-2.0-or-later. Their parts that came from the fork are written again from public texts, by writers
that had not seen the earlier code, against a contract of interfaces and behaviour:

- dvbridge_metadata.h: the 44 parts of the serializer of ETSI GS CCM 001 V1.1.1 clause 6 (the
  dm_metadata() payload of 6.2, the transport packets and their CRC of 6.3). Hades' own parts are
  kept as they were, character for character.
- mpv_dvbridge_cm4.h, whole: the conversion of the blocks of levels 3, 4, 8 to 11 and 254 for the
  tunnel, from the field layouts of dovi_tool (MIT).
- pack_gles300.frag, whole: the packer of the composed way (BT.2020, BT.2100 narrow range at
  12 bits, CCM 001 6.4, the HDMI YCbCr 4:2:2 12-bit pixel encoding).
- dvbridge_render.c: skip_inactive_area() (the bars written first, the "Opt1" idea) and
  pack_active_area() (the one pass of the converted transport). The rest of the file is the
  fork's renderer adapter, now with the header of the module's other files from the fork.

Nothing changes in what the module sends. Measured against 8434d00:
- transport, on the software bridge (zink on lavapipe): 136 of 136 files the same, both ways, in
  the source and the converted transport, with YCbCr and IPT, step-down, the GUI over the picture
  and read in place, chroma siting, profile 5, end-of-signal frames (also with black codes set by
  hand), the packer with and without quad operations and the composer off; the HDR10 render, 3 of 3;
- the serializer test of 1.0 RC4: 255 frames, every payload read back from its packets byte for byte,
  and every end-of-signal packet the same;
- cm40_test: 26 of 26 checks, the 52 v4.0 blocks of its payloads the same bytes;
- a random test of the serializer and the conversion against the earlier ones: 21.5 million cases
  (11 million frames, 7 million blocks, 3.5 million calls of the other functions), every result
  the same; it runs every line of the two files but seven that cannot be reached;
- seven mutations of the new code, each one found.

The four files are under GPL-2.0-or-later.
